* OS-9 System Startup Script* Preloads the routinely-needed modules into the module directory so they* run from any account regardless of its execution directory (F$Load only* searches the exec dir), then hands off to tsmon for login.*setenv PATH /dd/CMDS:/dd/CMDS/SHARE* -- C runtime, assembler/linker, BASIC09 runtime, common file utilities* math881 is the 68881 hardware-FPU build of the math module: same module* name ("math"), so it is a drop-in replacement. Verified more accurate --* software math is wrong at the 7th significant digit on transcendentals* (sin(1)=.841471104 vs correct .841470985); with math881 sin/sqrt/pi/div* come out bit-exact and exp within ~2 ULP, matching real 68881 hardware.load cio csl math881load r68 l68 o68 runbload dir mdir del deldir copy makdirload cc cpp c68 gcc2 cccp2 cc2echo OS-9 Ready -- modules loaded* -- timesharing monitor: waits for a keypress on /term, then runs logintsmon /term